            <ArticleTitle>Separating wheat from chaff: examining the obesity paradox in the critically ill.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>168</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/cc12798</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity is an increasing burden globally. In the general population, the obese have an increased mortality risk. Regarding the critically ill, a growing body of literature supports the obesity paradox, the notion that obesity confers a protective effect in certain disease states. However, the paucity of methodologically sound trials prevents definitive interpretation and may obscure risks.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
